<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's KFA buys 52,000T of U.S. corn - traders.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's KFA buys 52,000T of U.S. corn - traders.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Korea Feed Association (KFA) bought 52,000 tonnes of U.S. No.3 yellow corn at $158 per tonne C&amp;F, traders said on Thursday.</p>
<p>They said the KFA bought the corn from Cargill in a private negotiation late on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Arrival was set for February 15 at the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822)727 5651</p>
